{"r":"raw","i":2,"ch":"screen","at":399972,"wallAt":1793660084781,"data":{"capture":{"lines":["","  Earth turns through these bulges once a day, so most coastlines get two high tides and two low tides. The","  Moon also moves along its orbit as Earth spins, so a full tidal cycle takes about 24 hours and 50 minutes.","  That's why high tide comes roughly 50 minutes later each day. The Sun causes tides too, but its effect is a","  bit less than half the Moon's. When the Sun, Moon and Earth line up at new and full moon, their pulls combine","  into extra-large spring tides. When they sit at right angles, during the quarter moons, they partly cancel","  and give milder neap tides.","  Real tides are messier than this simple picture. The shape of coastlines, ocean basins and the seafloor can","  slow tides down, amplify them or redirect them. Some places get only one high tide a day, and Canada's Bay of","  Fundy has tides over 15 meters high.","  ❯ /clear                                      Start a new session with empty context; previous session","                                                stays on disk (resumable with /resume)","───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","❯ /clear","───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","  ⏸ manual mode on"],"status":{"exists":true,"dead":false,"exitStatus":null,"exitSignal":null,"inMode":false,"alternateOn":false,"cursorX":0,"cursorY":15,"cols":111,"rows":24,"historySize":0},"at":399972,"hash":"25e8b9bbf123262e"}}}
